<title>HUNGARY: GE's BB reports HUF 4.68 bln group after-tax.</title>
<headline>GE's BB reports HUF 4.68 bln group after-tax.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				     Jan-Dec 1996    Jan-Dec 1996</p>
<p>				     (Bank only)   (consolidated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		6,706   vs    7,164</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  6,680   vs    6,375</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		5,218   vs    4,679</p>
<p>    Interest revenue	     46,015   vs   46,038</p>
<p>    Interest expenditure	 28,811   vs   29,061</p>
<p>    Dividend received		  28   vs	 37</p>
<p>    Other operating revenue    11,312   vs   10,999</p>
<p>    Other revenue		   7,628   vs    7,588</p>
<p>    Other operating expend.     4,898   vs    4,981</p>
<p>    Other expenditure	    13,277   vs   13,104</p>
<p>    Operating costs		11,291   vs   10,352</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income	 84 loss vs    17 loss</p>
<p>    Taxation			  1,462   vs    1,696</p>
<p>NOTE - Budapest Bank Rt is controlled by General Electric Capital Services, the financial arm of the GE group. Budapest Bank shareholders will hold their annual general meeting on April 30, 0900 GMT, in the Budapest Congress Center.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
